message: "Please cite the paper for the research findings; cite the software version when using the implementation or reproduction workflows."
type: software
title: "pico-WAM: A Compact World Action Model"
authors:
  - family-names: Pandya
    given-names: Keivalya
    affiliation: Northeastern University
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-29
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/keivalya/pico-wam"
url: "https://github.com/keivalya/pico-wam"
abstract: >-
  pico-WAM is a compact World Action Model for inspecting interactions between
  a learned policy, action-conditioned dynamics, and trajectory scoring.
  The repository provides Push-T experiments, a separate door-opening study,
  archived numerical evidence, and executable reproduction workflows.
  The controlled Push-T study supplies physical state at inference.
keywords:
  - world action models
  - world models
  - robot learning
  - model-based planning
  - counterfactual prediction
  - trajectory scoring
  - imitation learning
  - Push-T
